# Aesthetics Ranking — Project Conventions

## Stack
- Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
- Supabase (anonymous auth + RLS), `@supabase/ssr` for SSR-safe clients

## Architecture
- `src/lib/guarded-insertion.ts` — ranking algorithm (Guarded Top-5 Insertion). Do NOT replace with ELO or merge sort.
- `src/hooks/useSession.ts` — wraps the algorithm + Supabase persistence.
- `src/hooks/useSwipe.ts` — swipe phase (like/skip). State stored in localStorage.
- localStorage keys: `aesthetics_insertion_state_v1`, `aesthetics_insertion_pool_v1`, `aesthetics_likes_v2`, `aesthetics_swipe_index_v2`, `aesthetics_session_id`.

## Rules
- Never add `item.rating`, `item.wins`, `item.losses` — ELO is gone; use `item.rank`.
- `useSession(likedIds)` must be called **once per page**. Do not create a second instance just to fetch aesthetics — load aesthetics separately with `createClient().from("aesthetics").select("*")`.
- `clearSession()` must clear all localStorage keys listed above.
- Always use `unoptimized` on `<Image>` for CARI cover images (external domain).
- Supabase env vars: always add `?? "https://placeholder.supabase.co"` / `?? "placeholder"` to prevent build-time crashes.

## Comparisons budget
The guarded insertion algorithm guarantees ~18–30 comparisons for N=10–15 liked items. Do not add hard caps or ELO-style confidence thresholds — the algorithm terminates naturally.
